\f1\b\fs48 Quake-trance and the Order of the Perpetual Drop\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::1>
\f1\b Quake-trance
\f2\b0  is a predominantly infrasonic form of psychedelic electronic music which emerged in the American Southwest during the late twenty-second century and later developed into the principal liturgical practice of the 
\f1\b Order of the Perpetual Drop
\f2\b0 . The genre is distinguished by the incorporation of spinning Gyges discs into live performances so that parts of the surrounding physical environment participate in the music.\
The Order recognises three principal gods\'97
\f1\b Ludwig
\f2\b0 , 
\f1\b Zildjian
\f2\b0  and 
\f1\b Rickenbacker
\f2\b0 \'97and traditionally employs three Gyges discs during a full religious service, one for each deity. Lesser gods include 
\f1\b Pearl
\f2\b0 , 
\f1\b Gibson
\f2\b0  and 
\f1\b H\'f6fner
\f2\b0 , although these had fallen sufficiently far from fashion by the time of the Goa period to be dismissed by younger devotees as 
\f3\i so last Hootenanny
\f2\i0 .\
Quake-trance is best known outside its surviving religious communities for the 
\f1\b Rotherhithe Stasis Collapse
\f2\b0 , during which a particularly successful service in Goa produced a remote stasis-field event in London, several thousand kilometres away. The incident permanently altered international stasis-safety practice and briefly made Rickenbacker the only known god whose existence had generated paperwork at Fridge Force.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Musical characteristics\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 Quake-trance developed from several branches of psychedelic trance, especially progressive psytrance, forest psy and darker psychedelic techno. Its most significant innovation was to abandon the centuries-long competition to make trance faster and instead make it lower.\
By the time of the genre\'92s emergence, extremely fast psytrance had already demonstrated that a musical style could become more intense by adding beats until the human nervous system ceased distinguishing rhythm from emergency. Early quake-trance producers took the opposite position. Speed, they argued, was spiritually vulgar. The truly interesting part of music began below the range of hearing.\
A conventional quake-trance performance consequently contains two overlapping rhythmic systems.\
The audience generally hears a rolling four-on-the-floor pulse in the broad range of 128\'96138 beats per minute, accompanied by bass sequencing, sparse percussion and psychedelic electronic textures inherited from earlier trance traditions. Beneath this audible layer, one or more Gyges discs generate much lower oscillations, including infrasonic frequencies which are perceived through floors, bodies, loose objects and surrounding geology.\
A commonly quoted description of the genre is:\

\f1\b The people dance to the beat. The earth dances to the remainder.
\f2\b0 \
A performance typically begins with ordinary electronic instrumentation while the Gyges frequencies are introduced gradually. Over ten or twenty minutes, listeners may begin to feel vibration through their feet, ribs or teeth. Dust loosens. Tent poles hum. Stones chatter against one another. Vehicles occasionally acquire rhythm sections without consulting their owners.\
The moment at which the environment begins visibly responding is known as 
\f1\b the Drop
\f2\b0 .\
This use of 
\f3\i drop
\f2\i0  differs from the much older electronic-music term for the return of a beat after a period of tension. In orthodox quake-trance, a Drop is considered to have occurred only when something outside the sound system joins the performance.\
Traditional classifications include 
\f1\b club quake
\f2\b0 , regarded by purists as fraudulent because buildings are designed to vibrate; 
\f1\b festival quake
\f2\b0 , accepted for inexperienced listeners; 
\f1\b canyon quake
\f2\b0 , the orthodox desert form; and 
\f1\b tectonic quake
\f2\b0 , an advanced practice notable for having almost no surviving insurers.\

\f1\b Recorded quake
\f2\b0  is generally considered a contradiction in terms. The traditional argument is that if the geology is not live, neither is Ludwig.\

\f1\b Wet quake-trance
\f2\b0 , developed much later in Goa, was initially treated as decadent heresy and subsequently became the most technically significant branch of the genre.\
The influence of forest psytrance is particularly visible in quake-trance\'92s relationship with landscape. Forest psy had incorporated natural sounds and environmental textures into electronic music. Quake-trance musicians regarded sampling the environment as unnecessary modesty and instead developed methods for making the environment perform.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Origins in the American Southwest\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The precise origins of quake-trance remain disputed, in part because nearly every important early participant was attending an illegal desert party at the time and therefore had professional reasons to remember events differently.\
The genre arose from the growing availability of obsolete stasis equipment during the late twenty-second century. Complete stasis refrigeration units retained commercial value and were therefore rarely abandoned. Older Gyges assemblies were another matter. Their containment systems were obsolete, their control hardware was increasingly incompatible with modern infrastructure, and many had been manufactured by companies which had since been absorbed by other companies which were themselves eventually absorbed by pension funds.\
Desert artists acquired them cheaply.\
The initial attraction appears to have been simple. A spinning Gyges disc could produce extremely deep physical oscillations which conventional subwoofers could imitate only by being larger, more expensive and briefly illegal.\
The first recognised experiments took place in the Morongo Basin and surrounding desert communities. Dry rock proved particularly responsive. In saturated ground, low-frequency energy could vanish into complex coupled systems; in desert canyons it announced itself theatrically. Cliff faces hummed, stones danced, fissures shed dust and exposed rock made it obvious when somebody had succeeded.\
The Southwest also possessed two other essential resources: empty land and people who regarded safety instructions as a challenge category.\
The absence of nearby residents was especially valued by promoters, as neighbours and government regulators share the unfortunate habit of objecting when a bass line registers on seismic-monitoring equipment.\
Contemporary industry literature also noted one important commercial advantage of the desert: if something went catastrophically wrong, fewer lawyers could hear it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 The First Drop controversy\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 At least three locations claim an important role in the invention of quake-trance.\
The most widely accepted tradition places the 
\f1\b First Drop
\f2\b0  somewhere between Joshua Tree and Twentynine Palms. According to this version, an outdoor progressive-psy party was using two salvaged Gyges assemblies alongside a conventional sound system. One disc drifted slightly outside its expected operating range, followed soon afterwards by the second.\
Nothing spectacular happened at the equipment.\
A sandstone wall approximately eighty metres away began humming.\
The audience stopped dancing.\
The DJ, displaying the instincts later considered essential to the founding of a religion, did not stop the music.\
He changed the tempo.\
The humming grew stronger.\
People placed their hands against the rock and felt the pulse returning through their palms. Several later accounts claimed the canyon appeared to breathe. Another claimed that somebody shouted that 
\f1\b Ludwig had answered
\f2\b0 , although the identity of the person concerned was lost surprisingly early.\
Within six months, there were T-shirts.\
The original party invitation survived much longer than the location:\

\f1\b DRIVE EAST UNTIL YOUR NAV STOPS AGREEING WITH ITSELF.
\f2\b0 \

\f1\b TURN LEFT AT THE BURNT SOFA.
\f2\b0 \
The existence of several burnt sofas in the area complicated later pilgrimage. The situation deteriorated when local property owners began adding additional burnt sofas to improve the spiritual credentials of otherwise unremarkable land.\
Eventually seven separate sites claimed to be the First Drop canyon.\
All charged admission.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Slab City tradition\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 The Slab City school rejects the Joshua Tree account and credits the invention of quake-trance to an engineer or refrigeration technician known as 
\f1\b Manny No-Last-Name
\f2\b0 .\
According to Slab tradition, Manny connected a stolen Gyges regulator to a bass system because he needed \'93more bottom\'94.\
Manny was later canonised by several local groups.\
The Order of the Perpetual Drop refused to recognise him, partly because surviving foundational accounts alternately describe Manny as one man, three brothers, a woman, and a collective pseudonym adopted by anybody who had rewired electrical equipment while intoxicated.\
Slab quake remained stylistically raw. Technical competence was widely regarded as evidence of commercial compromise. Exposed wiring was doctrinal. Intact safety housings were grounds for suspicion.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Arcosanti school\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f2 Arcosanti entered quake-trance history somewhat later and is generally credited with giving the genre its first coherent theory.\
Researchers there noticed that the strength and location of environmental responses depended on the spacing, orientation and timing of multiple Gyges fields. This led to the first deliberately engineered canyon-scale Drops and the formal study of standing-wave geometry in quake-trance performance.\
The Arcosanti school described its practitioners as 
\f1\b geo-composers
\f2\b0 .\
Everybody hated Arcosanti.\
The results remained difficult to argue with.\
A later summary of the early movement observed that Joshua Tree gave quake-trance its soul, Slab City claimed to have given it its balls, and Arcosanti gave it equations.\
This was regarded as unfair to Joshua Tree by Slab City and unfair to mathematics by Arcosanti.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Development of the theology\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 Ludwig, Zildjian and Rickenbacker did not begin as gods.\
They began as brand names.\
The 
\f1\b Great Silicon Meltdown
\f2\b0  of the mid-twenty-first century destroyed a substantial proportion of surviving American cultural records when data centres across the Lower States failed in a cascading thermal disaster. Music archives, films, literature, correspondence, photographs and several centuries of popular culture disappeared.\
Financial records had naturally been replicated elsewhere.\
Physical artefacts survived much better than their explanations.\
Among these were drum kits marked 
\f1\b LUDWIG
\f2\b0 , cymbals bearing 
\f1\b ZILDJIAN
\f2\b0 , and electric guitars and basses carrying the name 
\f1\b RICKENBACKER
\f2\b0 . Archaeological images also survived showing enormous crowds facing illuminated platforms upon which people manipulated these objects while the audience displayed behaviours readily interpreted as collective religious ecstasy.\
Several archaeomusicologists proposed that Ludwig, Zildjian and Rickenbacker had simply been manufacturers.\
The theory explained nearly everything.\
It was therefore dismissed as reductive.\
Quake-trance had already adopted the three names as performance slang. A particularly strong kick might be described as Ludwig arriving. Uncontrolled metallic vibration indicated Zildjian\'92s approval. When infrasonic energy travelled unusually well through the ground, performers would say that Rickenbacker was listening.\
Everyone initially understood these remarks as jokes.\
This condition proved temporary.\
At one frequently cited canyon performance, a rock face continued vibrating after the audible music stopped. Somebody announced that Rickenbacker was still listening.\
People laughed.\
Twenty years later they were still saying it.\
Fifty years later it was traditional.\
Someone wrote it down.\
Another person wrote explanatory notes.\
The explanatory notes became canonical.\
The joke became heresy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 The principal gods\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2><$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Ludwig\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b Ludwig
\f2\b0 , later styled the God of the First Impact, governs pulse, thunder, impact and the initiation of resonance.\
His symbol is the circle within a circle, derived from the bass drum.\
Orthodox services begin with Ludwig because vibration must first be struck into existence. His clergy developed primarily from percussionists, some of whom became known as 
\f1\b Luddites
\f2\b0 , causing centuries of difficulty for historians attempting to distinguish religious personnel from opponents of technology.\
Ludwig supplies the beat.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Zildjian\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b Zildjian
\f2\b0 , God of the Breaking Sky, governs high-frequency chaos, metallic violence, fracture, revelation and the moment at which a stable structure becomes interesting.\
His surviving sacred objects are bronze discs derived from ancient cymbals.\
Zildjian\'92s principal theological contribution is 
\f1\b the Crash
\f2\b0 .\
A Drop may begin with Ludwig and descend towards Rickenbacker, but Zildjian traditionally marks the moment when events exceed the insurance policy.\
Zildjian supplies the rupture.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 <$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b\fs28 Rickenbacker\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 <!$Scr_H::3>
\f1\b Rickenbacker
\f2\b0 , usually styled the God Beneath, is the most important deity in later quake-trance theology.\
He governs low frequencies, subterranean communication, buried things, distant sympathetic vibration and anything felt before it is heard.\
The Order teaches that Rickenbacker lives beneath the crust.\
This produced a theological explanation for long-range resonance which became considerably less funny after Rotherhithe.\
Rickenbacker, the doctrine states, does not need to travel from one place to another.\

\f1\b He is already underneath both places.
\f2\b0 \
Physicists generally disliked this explanation because, annoyingly, it predicted several observations about as successfully as the available equations.\
Rickenbacker supplies the resonance.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Lesser gods and the Hootenanny problem\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The lesser pantheon includes Pearl, Gibson and H\'f6fner, each of whom appears to have held greater status during earlier periods.\

\f1\b Pearl
\f2\b0  was Ludwig\'92s principal rival during the Great Drum Schism. The doctrinal distinction between the two movements is lost; surviving texts indicate that both sides believed passionately in the supreme spiritual importance of drums.\

\f1\b Gibson
\f2\b0  governs excess, heroic display and solos. The Gibson tradition once occupied a major place in guitar-heavy forms of early quake-trance, particularly performances in which one participant continued playing after everyone else had made it clear they were finished.\

\f1\b H\'f6fner
\f2\b0  became associated with levitation, lightness and improbable bass frequencies. Surviving iconography frequently depicts a revered but unidentified ancient saint holding a violin-shaped bass.\
By the mature period, Pearl, Gibson and H\'f6fner were dismissed as 
\f1\b so last Hootenanny
\f2\b0 .\
The meaning of 
\f3\i Hootenanny
\f2\i0  had already been lost.\
Theologians agreed that it had been an ancient American ceremony but disagreed over whether it involved communal music, ecstatic dancing, ritual combat, animal sacrifice or competitive knitwear.\
No evidence has ever eliminated competitive knitwear.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 The Order of the Perpetual Drop\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The Order developed gradually from the religious language of quake-trance rather than appearing as a separate movement.\
Early performers used phrases such as \'93Rickenbacker is awake tonight\'94 to mean the bass response was unusually good, or \'93Ludwig wants another one\'94 when the audience wanted another track. \'93Zildjian approves\'94 commonly followed the discovery that some piece of nearby metalwork had begun vibrating.\
Scene mythology followed.\
Then irony.\
Then people arrived who failed to understand that the irony was irony.\
Many excellent religions have developed similarly.\
During the early twenty-third century, a group of purists accused commercial quake-trance of abandoning its spiritual foundations and founded the 
\f1\b Order of the Perpetual Drop
\f2\b0 .\
Other performers initially assumed the Order was performance art.\
The Order interpreted this as persecution.\
This proved decisive.\
The mature Order formalised a service around three Gyges discs, one dedicated to each principal god. Ludwig established the fundamental pulse; Zildjian introduced instability and harmonic complexity; Rickenbacker brought the resulting field towards coherence with the surrounding landscape.\
The final stage was the 
\f1\b Perpetual Drop
\f2\b0 , when the environment became part of the composition.\
The Order taught that a successful Drop continued beneath the earth after the audible performance ended, propagating outward indefinitely until another part of the world responded.\
For almost a century this doctrine was metaphorical.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Commercialisation of the American desert\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 Quake-trance\'92s transformation from obscure desert music into a profitable cultural movement was viewed by the Order as its first great catastrophe.\
A genuine Drop was difficult to produce, potentially dangerous and impossible to schedule reliably.\
Commercial Drops could be offered at 8:15, 9:30 and 11:00.\
Resorts appeared throughout the principal desert regions and began offering 
\f1\b Authentic First Drop Experiences
\f2\b0 , 
\f1\b Ludwig Thunder Massage
\f2\b0 , 
\f1\b Zildjian Resonance Cleansing
\f2\b0 , 
\f1\b Rickenbacker Subterranean Couples Therapy
\f2\b0  and 
\f1\b Junior Quake
\f2\b0 , recommended for ages eight to fourteen.\
High-end retreats introduced 
\f1\b Zero-Risk Tectonic Spirituality
\f2\b0 .\
Decorative Gyges discs rotated safely beside meditation rooms while hidden transducers shook the floor.\
Guests received certificates confirming that the Earth had moved for them.\
Canyon landowners began charging 
\f1\b resonance premiums
\f2\b0 , calculated according to cliff height, geological composition and proximity to historically significant cracks.\
Luxury housing appeared around favoured resonant basins.\
The Order complained bitterly, although sales of Order-branded clothing performed extremely well.\
The final breach occurred when a luxury wellness company registered 
\f1\b The Perpetual Drop Experience\'99
\f2\b0 .\
The Order convened an emergency council.\
After several days, two schisms, an assault involving a ceremonial cymbal and an unresolved debate over whether bottled mineral water could participate in a geological sacrament, the American desert was declared 
\f1\b SPIRITUALLY OVERDEVELOPED
\f2\b0 .\
The Order sought somewhere the gods had not yet been franchised.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Relocation to Goa\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The Order eventually acquired a bankrupt trance ashram in Goa whose previous owners had failed to monetise enlightenment.\
The choice contained an historical irony almost completely invisible to the participants.\
Psychedelic trance itself descended in part from the Goa trance tradition of the late twentieth century. Centuries of cultural loss had erased this ancestry from common knowledge. Quake-trance therefore travelled from a remote descendant of Goa trance, through centuries of musical mutation, to the American desert, where it developed into an apparently indigenous geological religion.\
The Order then congratulated itself on discovering Goa.\
Nobody realised they had gone home.\
The former ashram offered a large performance chamber, substantial electrical capacity, sea views and neighbours whose long exposure to trance music had exhausted the normal human repertoire of complaint.\
It possessed one serious disadvantage.\
It was wet.\
Traditional quake-trance was a dry-rock tradition. The American canyon acted as a sounding board: energy entered exposed geology, produced a visible response and stayed reassuringly close to the people responsible.\
Goa provided saturated laterite, groundwater, estuarine mud, monsoon rainfall, humid air and direct access to the Arabian Sea.\
Traditionalists declared the environment acoustically unsuitable.\
The Order announced the invention of 
\f1\b Wet Quake-Trance
\f2\b0 .\
Older members called it heresy until the first season sold out.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Wet quake-trance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The acoustic behaviour of the Goa site transformed the genre.\
The saturated laterite coupled readily with groundwater. Groundwater interacted with estuarine sediment. The estuary connected with tidal channels, and tidal channels possessed access to an Arabian Sea whose interest in the performance had not been sought.\
Instead of behaving like a hard sounding board, the local environment behaved increasingly like an enormous coupled membrane.\
Early Wet Drops produced slower and deeper environmental responses than their American equivalents.\
Floors shifted gently.\
Coconut palms shivered without wind.\
Standing water formed concentric ripples.\
Glasses migrated across tables.\
A good American Drop could make a canyon wall hum.\
A good Goan Drop could make a palm tree shake half a kilometre away.\
A better one produced rings in standing water without an obvious centre.\
An exceptional one caused the estuary to reconsider which direction the sea was in.\
Devotees concluded that 
\f1\b Rickenbacker was more communicative in the tropics
\f2\b0 .\
Attendance increased rapidly.\
So did the power allocated to the three discs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 The Goa Service and the Rotherhithe Stasis Collapse\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The service responsible for the Rotherhithe Collapse used the orthodox three-disc arrangement.\
One disc belonged to Ludwig.\
One belonged to Zildjian.\
One belonged to Rickenbacker.\
The performance began shortly after sunset and was regarded by surviving members as one of the finest in the Order\'92s history.\
Ludwig established the pulse.\
Zildjian introduced increasingly complex interactions.\
Rickenbacker brought the three fields towards coherence with the surrounding wet geology.\
The floor moved.\
The building hummed.\
Palms shook.\
Water responded hundreds of metres from the performance space.\
Witnesses along the estuary described a vibration passing beneath their feet.\
The congregation interpreted this as enthusiastic divine participation and continued.\
The three fields eventually entered a highly coherent state.\
For several minutes the Order experienced what later accounts described as the finest Perpetual Drop ever achieved.\
One witness said it felt as though the planet had become hollow.\
Another described the universe clearing its throat.\
Goa had a memorable evening.\
Rotherhithe slid into the Thames.\
No relevant stasis facility existed in Rotherhithe. No industrial accident had occurred nearby. No experimental field equipment was operating in the district.\
Buildings shifted.\
Foundations failed.\
Sections of riverbank moved.\
Then the Thames developed a hump.\
The official investigation later called this an 
\f1\b anomalous standing hydraulic elevation
\f2\b0 , because investigators had professional standards.\
For several minutes, a considerable quantity of the river rose above the surrounding river and remained there. Boats sat at angles not contemplated by their designers. Two tide gauges registered high tide simultaneously within the same stretch of water.\
The Port Authority initially discarded one reading because its software permitted only one Thames.\
The hump subsequently collapsed.\
A sightseeing boat was deposited on the roof of a riverside car park.\
Its automated commentary continued throughout the event because the ticket conditions contained no provision for geological ascension.\
The Order learned of Rotherhithe later that evening and immediately attributed the event to Rickenbacker.\
British investigators did not.\
Fridge Force did not.\
Indian authorities did not.\
The suggestion that a religious rave in Goa had destroyed part of London was considered an unattractive hypothesis, particularly by officials who had already announced several more respectable ones.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Fridge Force investigation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The Rotherhithe investigation lasted nearly a year and involved three international inquiries.\
The decisive evidence came from surviving telemetry recorded at Goa and field signatures captured around London. Investigators eventually demonstrated that the three Gyges fields in Goa had entered an exceptionally coherent configuration at almost exactly the time Rotherhithe began experiencing the anomalous effects.\
The mathematics remained difficult.\
Distance proved surprisingly unimportant.\
Relative phase mattered.\
Geometry mattered.\
Coherence mattered.\
The final model indicated that the three fields in Goa had behaved as a single combined system whose strongest physical manifestation occurred around Rotherhithe.\
Fridge Force eventually classified the incident as a 
\f1\b multidimensionally colocated resonant concurrency event
\f2\b0 , a term which successfully avoided saying that Goa and Rotherhithe had briefly become the same place.\
The region around London was described as a 
\f1\b remote resonance locus
\f2\b0 .\
Rotherhithe had been sitting in it.\
The discovery transformed stasis engineering. Shielding requirements were rewritten, minimum separation rules introduced and the deliberate interaction of multiple independent stasis fields became one of the few technical practices Fridge Force regarded with less enthusiasm than espionage.\
The Order offered its own explanation.\
Rickenbacker did not need to transmit anything from Goa to London.\
He was already beneath both.\
The physicists found this irritating.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \strokec2 <$Scr_H::2>
\f1\b\fs36 Closed resonance anomaly\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec2 <!$Scr_H::2>
\f2 The final Rotherhithe report contained one anomaly which attracted little attention outside the most highly classified technical appendices.\
Immediately before the Goa configuration collapsed, three independent instruments registered a resonance returning through the generating array.\
The returning signal closely matched the pattern being produced by the three discs.\
Its phase was reversed.\
Its amplitude was slightly greater.\
Its timing was impossible.\
The return signal had arrived before the corresponding source signal was generated.\
Investigators repeatedly checked the clocks.\
The clocks remained offensive.\
Reconstruction of the field geometry produced an additional result. During the same fraction of a second, the calculated remote resonance locus ceased to be remote.\
It briefly coincided with the generating apparatus in Goa.\
The appendix author called the condition 
\f1\b closed resonance
\f2\b0 .\
The three Gyges discs used by the Order had occupied fixed positions, and the condition vanished almost immediately as their coherence failed. No subsequent test reproduced it.\
The appendix ended with a warning.\
A system capable of changing the relative geometry of its generating fields continuously while maintaining coherence might sustain conditions which the fixed Goa apparatus could only pass through accidentally.\
}